# q069 filter_in_fkref_dataset — promoted from A3 probe-02 (audit item 7, F-AUD-5)
# Coverage: a bounded FILTER(?fk IN (...)) over an FK-REF var. Item 7 lowers a
#   bounded IN/VALUES set to an Iceberg Expression::In for scalar-column POMs; an
#   FK-IRI IN (this shape) still declines to prune (the FK-key template reversal is
#   a documented follow-on), so here it is a PARITY member (native==virtual) and a
#   pruning member once FK-IRI lowering lands. The scalar prune win is shown by q070.
# Exec path: query_from() FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main> (the deployed solo/chat shape).
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?oid ?tot
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?o a edw:Order ; edw:orderId ?oid ; edw:orderTotal ?tot ; edw:store ?st .
        FILTER(?st IN (<http://data.fluree.dev/edw/store/1>,
                       <http://data.fluree.dev/edw/store/2>,
                       <http://data.fluree.dev/edw/store/3>)) }
